title: Veeam: Backup Proxies
agents: special
catalog: os/storage
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors a backup proxy of a Veeam Backup & Replication server,
 collected via the Veeam special agent. Its summary shows the proxy's three
 conditions and its type; the details show its description and host.

 A proxy has three independent conditions, always shown in the order below.
 A proxy can be online and disabled, or offline and enabled, at the same
 time.

 Connection ({Online} or {Offline}): whether the backup server can reach
 the proxy. An offline proxy is {CRIT}, since it cannot run a backup,
 unless it is disabled; then the configured state for a disabled proxy
 applies instead.

 Admin state ({Enabled} or {Disabled}): whether the proxy has been
 disabled in Veeam, so that no backups are assigned to it. A disabled
 proxy is {OK} by default; the state is configurable, since a deliberately
 disabled proxy is normal in some estates.

 Components ({Up to date} or {Out of date}): whether the Veeam components
 installed on the proxy match the backup server's version. Out-of-date
 components are {WARN}.

 The type is one of: a VMware proxy ("VMware vSphere"), which processes
 backups of VMware vSphere virtual machines; a Hyper-V off-host proxy
 ("Hyper-V"), which takes the processing of Hyper-V backups off the
 Hyper-V hosts; or a general-purpose proxy ("General purpose"), which is
 used for agent, file share and object storage backups.

discovery:
 One service is created for each backup proxy reported by the API.

item:
 The name of the backup proxy.
